 \boxed{friend\_mary = 40 * 2 = \underline{\boxed{80}}}

 2. Next, Mary received 18 new potted plants from the nursery, so she now has a total of:
 updated_mary = friend_mary + nursery
 \boxed{updated\_mary = 80 + 18 = \underline{\boxed{98}}}

 3. Finally, Mary has decided to give away 1 potted plant from each of her 40 window ledges, removing a total of:
 given_plants = plants_per_ledge * ledges
 \boxed{given\_plants = 2 * 40 = \underline{\boxed{80}}}

 4. After giving away these plants, Mary will be left with:
 remaining_mary = updated_mary - given_plants
 \boxed{remaining\_mary = 98 - 80 = \underline{\boxed{18}}}

 Mary will remain with 18 potted plants after giving some away.
